For each claim below, decide whether its evidence quotes, on their own, support the claim.
- supported: the quotes state everything the claim asserts.
- partially_supported: the claim adds specifics (versions, impacts, scopes, causes) that the quotes do not state, but its core is supported.
- not_supported: the quotes do not support the claim, or contradict it.
In "missing", name what the claim adds beyond the quotes (empty string if supported).
Each claim lists the source document and section its quotes come from. That metadata is trustworthy: a quote taken from the "18.0.0" section of the changelog does establish that the change is in release 18, even if the quote does not repeat the version number.
Claims about the application or deployment (e.g. "The application uses X", "The cluster serves Y") are hypotheses that a downstream checker will test, not facts about a specific app. Judge them supported when the quotes establish that apps or deployments meeting the condition are affected; do not penalize them for lacking evidence about a particular application.

Claims (JSON):
[
 {
  "condition_id": "the_upgrade_crosses_postgresql_release_1_78cef0",
  "claim": "The upgrade crosses PostgreSQL release 16, where role inheritance became the default for member roles added during GRANT.",
  "evidence": [
   {
    "quote": "Role inheritance now controls the default inheritance status of member roles added during GRANT",
    "source": "PostgreSQL 16 release notes: Migration to Version 16",
    "release_of_change": "16"
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "condition_id": "the_application_or_administration_toolin_8cc43e",
  "claim": "The application or administration tooling changes a role's inheritance status (e.g. ALTER ROLE ... INHERIT/NOINHERIT) and relies on that change affecting existing memberships.",
  "evidence": [
   {
    "quote": "changes to a role's inheritance status affected all previous and future member roles",
    "source": "PostgreSQL 16 release notes: Migration to Version 16",
    "release_of_change": "16"
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "condition_id": "roles_with_non_default_inheritance_statu_d907a4",
  "claim": "Roles with non-default inheritance status (NOINHERIT) exist and have members granted, so memberships depend on the role's inheritance status.",
  "evidence": [
   {
    "quote": "Previously the inheritance status of member roles was controlled only by the role's inheritance status",
    "source": "PostgreSQL 16 release notes: Migration to Version 16",
    "release_of_change": "16"
   }
  ]
 }
]
